# Environment & Long-Term Memory

<!--
Copy to: $HERMES_DATA_DIR/memories/MEMORY.md

Infrastructure topology and durable facts the agent should know before it
starts poking around. Do not put secrets here — those belong in .env.
-->

## Hosts

- `pi` — Raspberry Pi 4 (4 GB RAM, arm64), Debian, Docker + Compose v2
  - Runs this Hermes stack (`~/projects/hermes-agent-stack`)
  - SSH: `ssh pi@192.168.1.10`
- `nas` — Synology, 192.168.1.20, SMB shares under `/volume1`

## Network

- LAN: `192.168.1.0/24`, gateway `192.168.1.1`
- DNS: Pi-hole at `192.168.1.5`
- No services are exposed directly to the internet; remote access is via
  WireGuard/Tailscale or an SSH tunnel.

## Services

- Hermes dashboard: `http://127.0.0.1:9119` on the host (loopback only)
- Home Assistant: `http://192.168.1.30:8123`
- Backups: nightly `restic` job to external USB disk

## Conventions

- Containers: `restart: unless-stopped`, pinned image tags, log rotation
- Secrets: `.env` files with mode `600`, never committed
- Before changing network or storage config, show a plan and wait for approval
